{
  "A menu bar of an app (File, Edit, View) and the menu that opens on a right-click. Both show the same menu items: submenus, check and radio items, shortcuts, access keys.": "",
  "MenuBar": "",
  "A `MenuBar` takes its top items as `items`; each one's `items` is its menu. `&File` makes Alt+F open File. Left and Right move along the bar and, while a menu is open, to the next menu; Escape goes back to the bar.": "",
  "Submenus, checks, radios, shortcuts": "",
  "An item with `items` opens a submenu at its side: Right (Left in a right-to-left page), Enter or Space open it, Left and Escape close it, and the pointer opens it after a short rest. `checked` makes a check item; `checked` with a `group` one choice of several, shown with a dot. `shortcut` is shown at the end of the item; register the key itself with `addShortcut`. The same items work in `Button`’s menu.": "",
  "The label; `&Copy` makes C choose it while the menu is open (Alt+C on a menu bar’s top item).": "",
  "An icon at the start, a tooltip.": "",
  "A key combination shown at the end (`Ctrl+S`). Only shown: register the key with `addShortcut`.": "",
  "A second, dimmer text after the label: what tells the item apart, such as a folder. Part of the item’s name, never a key.": "",
  "A submenu, opened at the side.": "",
  "A check item (`menuitemcheckbox`).": "",
  "With `checked`: one choice of a group (`menuitemradio`), shown with a dot.": "",
  "Dimmed and not chosen, or left out.": "",
  "The item in the kit tone color (`danger` for a destructive one); a toolbar button moved into the overflow menu keeps its tone.": "",
  "Chosen, after the menu closed. `e`: `{ item, source, event }`.": "",
  "ContextMenu": "",
  "A `ContextMenu` opens on its target’s right-click at the pointer, and with the Menu key or Shift+F10 at the focused element. `onOpening` gets the element (`e.target`) and builds the items for it, here for the row of a list; `e.cancel = true` leaves the browser its own menu. It closes on Escape and a press outside; when the page scrolls it goes along with the element it opened on, and closes once that element is out of sight.": "",
  "attachContextMenu": "",
  "Into the menu bar (one stop), and out of it.": "",
  "On the bar: the previous / next top item. In a menu: the neighbour’s menu, or close a submenu (Right opens one). Mirrored right to left.": "",
  "On the bar: open the menu, first item. Up opens it on the last item.": "",
  "In a menu: move between the items, wrapping around.": "",
  "The next item starting with it; an item’s `&` key chooses it.": "",
  "Opens the top item with that `&` key (Control + Option on Apple platforms).": "",
  "Closes a submenu, then the menu, back to where it opened.": "",
  "Focuses the menu bar, with `focusOnF10`.": "",
  "Opens a context menu at the focused element.": "",
  "`role=\"menubar\"` named by `label`; top items are `menuitem`s with `aria-haspopup` and `aria-expanded`, one Tab stop (roving tabindex).": "",
  "`role=\"menu\"`; items are `menuitem`, `menuitemcheckbox` or `menuitemradio` with `aria-checked`; disabled ones `aria-disabled`, still reachable.": "",
  "The item has `aria-haspopup=\"menu\"` and `aria-expanded`; the submenu opens next to it, focus goes in and comes back.": "",
  "A menu opened from the keyboard focuses its first item; from the pointer, the menu itself. Closing gives focus back.": "",
  "The shortcut text is part of the item’s name; access keys are in `aria-keyshortcuts` on the top items.": "",
  "Menus write no text of their own: every label, shortcut and name comes from your items, so they follow your own translations (a function in `text` follows a language change at once).": "",
  "The menu bar, its row, a top item (`aria-expanded=\"true\"` while open).": "",
  "The context menu (no box of its own) and the point it opens at.": "",
  "A menu (shared with Button), an item, a line.": "",
  "The parts of an item.": "",
  "The heights of the bar and of a top item.": "",
  "Units: the bar; a top item with its box per state (`hover`, `pressed`, `open`, `disabled`, `focus`); its icon; its access key’s mark (`shown`).": "",
  "Menu items (shared with Button’s menu): the item unit in each state (`highlight`, `pressed`, `focus`, `checked`, `disabled`, `first`, `last`, each tone and `<tone>-highlight`), the row height, whether a text wraps.": "",
  "Units: the column of items, the leading mark and icon, the check and radio marks, the line between groups.": "",
  "Units: an item’s text, its description, the shortcut and the submenu arrow.": "",
  "MenuBar props": "",
  "The top items; their `items` are the menus they open. A top item without `items` runs its `click`.": "",
  "Names the bar for screen readers. The same property as `text`.": "",
  "F10 moves focus to the bar from anywhere on the page. Off by default: browsers use F10.": "",
  "While a menu is open, pointing at another top item opens its menu; pointing at an item opens its submenu.": "",
  "ContextMenu props": "",
  "The commands; `onOpening` can give others per element.": "",
  "its parent": "",
  "Whose menu it is. Without it, the element the `ContextMenu` is placed in.": "",
  "Names the menu for screen readers.": "",
  "The Menu key and Shift+F10 open it at the focused element.": "",
  "Scrolling that takes the element it opened on out of sight closes it; until then the menu goes along with that element.": "",
  "Pointing at an item opens its submenu.": "",
  "`false`: the browser shows its own menu.": "",
  "The top item whose menu is open.": "",
  "The element it was last opened on.": "",
  "The element it listens on.": "",
  "Opens a top item’s menu with focus on its first item.": "",
  "Closes the open menu.": "",
  "Opens it programmatically, at `{ x, y }` or at an element.": "",
  "Your items may be plain or reactive; the menu reads them as they are. After changing them in place, call `refresh()`. The bar, the open menu and its submenus follow.": "",
  "Gives an element or component a menu; `items` can be a function of the opening (`e.target`). Returns the remover.": "",
  "Both: an item was chosen, after its own `click`.": "",
  "About to open. `e`: `{ target, items, cancel, byKeyboard, event, source }`; set `e.items` for the element, or `e.cancel = true`.": "",
  "`escape`, `outside`, `focus` or `code`.": ""
}
